#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/layout/ascend/index.rst:57
msgid ""
"Unlike :func:`make_ascend_nz_layout`, this layout does not round the row "
"extent of every leading stage up to 16.  A logical ``[..., rows, cols]`` "
"buffer is stored as consecutive ``[C0-group, rows, C0]`` blocks, with all "
"leading dimensions flattened into the C0-group axis.  Consequently, a padded "
"``rows = tile_rows + 1`` stage has exactly the source pitch expected by "
"``ascend_nd2nz_post_copy``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/layout/ascend/index.rst:65
msgid ""
"This layout is intended for UB data that is produced directly in NZ order "
"(for example with ``vsstb`` or a layout-driven ``T.copy``) and then copied "
"to L1. It is not an L1 Cube operand layout. For an ND-to-NZ ``T.copy``, the "
"allocation's row extent must include one trailing padding row while the "
"copied destination region excludes it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/layout/ascend/index.rst:76
msgid ""
"The contiguous reduce-K axis is grouped by C0 and is the outer physical "
"major: ``(.., mn, k) -> [.., k / C0, mn / 16, mn % 16, k % C0]``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/layout/ascend/index.rst:84
msgid ""
"The contiguous output M/N axis is grouped by C0 and is the outer physical "
"major: ``(.., k, mn) -> [.., mn / C0, k / 16, k % 16, mn % C0]``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/layout/ascend/index.rst:90
msgid ""
"Create the fixed Ascend L0C accumulator fractal layout for logical ``[.., M, "
"N]`` tiles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/layout/ascend/index.rst:93
msgid ""
"The physical shape is ``[.., N / 16, M / 16, 16, 16]`` and the forward map "
"is ``(.., m, n) -> [.., n / 16, m / 16, m % 16, n % 16]``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/layout/ascend/index.rst:101
msgid ""
"A logical ``[..., MN, K]`` scale tile maps to physical ``[..., MN/16, K / "
"(16 / dtype.bits), 16, 16 / dtype.bits]``. For uint8/int8 SF this is ``[..., "
"MN/16, K/2, 16, 2]``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/layout/ascend/index.rst:108
